---
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
import Documentation from '../layouts/Documentation.astro';
import {tokens} from '@klein-ui/tokens';
const colours=['klein-600','paper','band','tint','border','ink','body','good','watch','bad'] as const;
---
<Documentation title="Foundations"><main class="docs-catalogue"><h1>Exact by design.</h1><p>Klein blue is the accent. White is the ground. Geist carries interface text; Geist Mono carries measured values. Flat surfaces, square geometry and fine rules create structure.</p><div class="docs-swatches">{colours.map(name=><div><div class="docs-swatch" style={`background:var(--k-${name})`}></div><strong>{name}</strong><code>{tokens[name]}</code></div>)}</div><h2>Colour follows meaning</h2><p>A negative cost variance is not automatically bad. Pass the semantic consequence from your data layer. Supporting copy uses the body colour; muted colour is reserved for inactive controls.</p><h2>Atomic composition</h2><ol><li>Tokens: colour, typography, spacing and rules.</li><li>Atoms: buttons, icons and form controls.</li><li>Molecules: fields, tabs, page headers and section headings.</li><li>Organisms: table collection, chart with legend, metric strip, forecast and Eddy.</li><li>Templates: list, detail, dashboard and workspace layouts.</li></ol><h2>Layouts and extensions</h2><p>Edge-to-edge bands meet at their outer edges with no page padding or inter-band gaps. Each band owns its internal gutter. Flowstate's opt-in dark stylesheet and dark chart palette preserve product behaviour; the core reference is light.</p><h2>Token reference</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(tokens).map(([name,value])=><tr><th scope="row"><code>--k-{name}</code></th><td><code>{value}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></main></Documentation>
